#: theory.md:1
msgid "Theory"
msgstr "理論"

#: theory.md:3
msgid "Collective Variables"
msgstr "Collective Variables"

#: theory.md:5
msgid ""
"In most cases, it is impossible to extract clear information about a system "
"of interest by monitoring the Cartesian coordinates of all atoms directly, "
"especially if our system contains many atoms. Instead, it is possible to "
"monitor the system by defining functions of those coordinates that describe "
"the chemical properties that we are interested in. These functions are "
"called Collective Variables (CVs) and allow biasing specific degrees of "
"freedom or analyzing how those properties evolve. Plumed has numerous CVs "
"already implemented that can be used with ASE. For a complete explanation of"
" CVs implemented in Plumed, [go to this "
"link](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html)."
msgstr ""
"全原子の Cartesian "
"座標を直接監視して明確な情報を得るのは、特に大きな系では困難です。対象の化学的性質を記述する座標の関数、Collective Variables "
"(CVs) を定義すれば、特定自由度への Bias や時間変化の解析が容易になります。PLUMED の多数の CV を ASE "
"で使えます。[一覧](https://www.plumed.org/doc-v2.8/user-doc/html/colvarintro.html) "
"を参照してください。"

#: theory.md:16
msgid "Metadynamics"
msgstr "Metadynamics"

#: theory.md:18
msgid ""
"[Metadynamics](https://www.nature.com/articles/s42254-020-0153-0) is an "
"enhanced sampling method that allows exploring the configuration landscape "
"by adding cumulative bias in terms of some CVs. This bias is added each "
"$\\tau$ time lapse and usually its shape is Gaussian. In time t, the "
"accumulated bias is defined as"
msgstr ""
"[Metadynamics](https://www.nature.com/articles/s42254-020-0153-0) は、CV "
"の関数として Bias を蓄積し地形を探索する Enhanced Sampling 法です。通常 Gaussian を $\\tau$ ごとに加え、時刻"
" t の蓄積 Bias は、"

#: theory.md:37
msgid ""
"where $\\mathbf{s}$ is a set of collective variables, $\\sigma_i$ is the "
"width of the Gaussian related to the i-th collective variable, and *W(s, "
"t')* is the height of the Gaussian in time *t'*. In simple metadynamics, "
"*W(s, t')* is a constant, but in Well-Tempered Metadynamics, the height of "
"the Gaussians is lower where previous bias was added. This reduction in the "
"height of the new Gaussians decreases the error and avoids exploration "
"towards high free energy states that are thermodynamically irrelevant. The "
"height in time t' for Well-Tempered Metadynamics is"
msgstr ""
"$\\mathbf{s}$ は CV 集合、$\\sigma_i$ は i 番目の Gaussian 幅、*W(s, t')* は時刻 *t'* "
"の高さです。通常は *W(s, t')* 一定ですが、Well-Tempered では既存 Bias "
"のある場所で低くします。誤差を減らし、熱力学的に重要でない高自由エネルギー状態の探索を避けます。時刻 t' の高さは、"

#: theory.md:56
msgid ""
"with $W$ the maximum height of the Gaussians, $\\beta$ the inverse of the "
"thermal energy ($1/k_BT$) and $\\gamma$ a bias factor greater than one that "
"regulates how fast the height of the bias decreases: the higher the bias "
"factor, the slower the heights decrease. Note that when $\\gamma$ approaches"
" infinity, this equation becomes constant and simple metadynamics is "
"recovered. In contrast, when $\\gamma$ approaches zero, no bias is added, "
"which is the case of Molecular Dynamics."
msgstr ""
"$W$ は最大高さ、$\\beta$ は熱エネルギーの逆数 ($1/k_BT$)、$\\gamma$ は1超の Bias Factor "
"です。大きいほど高さがゆっくり減ります。$\\gamma$ が無限大なら一定になり通常 Metadynamics に戻ります。一方 $\\gamma$ "
"が0に近づくと Bias がなく、通常 MD になります。"

#: theory.md:64
msgid ""
"The addition of the bias potential produces an extra force in each atom, "
"such that the resultant force for the i-th atom is"
msgstr "BiasPotential により各原子に追加の力が働き、i 番目の合力は、"

#: theory.md:77
msgid ""
"where $F_i$ is the natural unbiased force, $R_i$ is the coordinate of the "
"atom, and the second term is the additional force due to the added bias."
msgstr "$F_i$ は Unbiased な力、$R_i$ は座標、第2項は Bias による追加の力です。"

#: theory.md:80
msgid ""
"Part of the power of metadynamics is that it can be used for exploring "
"conformations. Moreover, the accumulated bias converges to the free energy "
"surface ( $F(s)$ ),"
msgstr "Conformation 探索に加え、Bias と自由エネルギー表面（$F(s)$）の収束関係を得られます。"

